{{ q1.subtitle }}.

The NVD analyzed {{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_before_2025") }} of new CVEs within 30 days before 2025
({{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_before_2025_low") }} to {{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_before_2025_high") }}),
{{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_2025_to_change") }} from 2025 to the change
({{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_2025_to_change_low") }} to {{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_2025_to_change_high") }}),
and {{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_since_change") }} since
({{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_since_change_low") }} to {{ v("backlog.q1.share_30d_since_change_high") }}).
The fall came before the change: from the first period to the second the 30 day share moved
{{ v("backlog.q1.change_30d_before_2025_to_2025_to_change") }}
(adjusted p {{ v("backlog.q1.change_30d_before_2025_to_2025_to_change_p_adjusted") }}), and from the
second to the third {{ v("backlog.q1.change_30d_2025_to_change_to_since_change") }}
(adjusted p {{ v("backlog.q1.change_30d_2025_to_change_to_since_change_p_adjusted") }}). The
announcement in April named what had already been happening since 2024.

When the NVD does analyze a CVE it is quick: the median among those analyzed is
{{ v("backlog.q1.median_days_analyzed_before_2025") }} before 2025 and
{{ v("backlog.q1.median_days_analyzed_since_change") }} since the change. The delay is not slow
work; it is work not done. A CVE is judged at k days only once k days have passed, so the newest
months count only the CVEs old enough to judge.

The data lead would push back: a month whose CVEs have not all had 90 days is judged on fewer of
them, and the history before 2017 is dated by rule, not by event. Both are in the method; the
monthly table behind the chart has the count judged at each horizon beside each share.

